<title>FRANCE: YACHTING-ROUND-THE-WORLD RACE SETS OFF.</title>
<headline>YACHTING-ROUND-THE-WORLD RACE SETS OFF.</headline>
<dateline>LES SABLES D'OLONNE, France 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thirteen men and two women left this western port as the single-handed, round-the-world yacht race got under way on Sunday.</p>
<p>Competitors will spend over three months at sea and try to beat the world record of 109 days eight hours 48 minutes held by Frenchman Titouan Lamazou.</p>
<p>Bertand de Broc of France made the fastest start, closely followed by compatriot Yves Parlier, regarded as the favourite. The last race, won by Frenchman Alain Gautier in 1993, cost two lives.</p>
</text>
